# Source for the Front's heterogeneous coalition: Fakhreddin Azimi,
# Iran: The Crisis of Democracy, 1941–1953, ch. 5, pp. 250–267.
# The recurring committee work and its effects are counterfactual.
title: Membership and Local Committees
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: membership_committees_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; membership_committees_timer = 4

= Membership and Local Committees

The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} needs people
who can turn statements in Tehran into repeatable local
work. Its components disagree over whether those organizers should answer to a
common committee or remain within the organizations that recruited them.

This is a real structural choice: shared committees spread common methods,
while autonomous organizers reduce fears of absorption.

[? if committee_stage > 0: Existing work follows the “[+ committee_model +]”
model. A new decision will deepen or reverse that organizational direction. ?]

- @committees_shared
- @committees_autonomy
- @return_card

@committees_shared
title: Build shared local committees
subtitle: One resource maintains common offices that tie the four components together
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: {!
var repeated = Q.committee_model === "Shared local committees";
var mature = Q.committee_stage >= 2;
Q.committee_model = "Shared local committees";
Q.committee_stage += 1;
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.iran_party_organization += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.toilers_organization += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.independent_nationalists_organization += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.religious_network_organization += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.organizational_reach += mature ? 1 : 4;
if (repeated) {
    Q.toilers_dissent += 1;
    Q.religious_network_dissent += 1;
}
!}

The secretariat pays for common forms, meeting space, and a small circuit of
organizers who train local committees to report in the same way. Each
component receives access to machinery it could not have built as quickly
alone.

The shared network reaches farther, but it consumes scarce funds and leaves
the question of ultimate authority for a later meeting.
[? if committee_stage > 2: Most gains now come from maintaining offices and
replacing exhausted volunteers. Further centralization reaches fewer new
places while reviving the argument over who commands the shared machinery. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@committees_autonomy
title: Let each component direct its own organizers
subtitle: Each component keeps command of its own organizers; coordination remains a negotiation
on-arrival: {!
var repeated = Q.committee_model === "Autonomous component organizers";
var mature = Q.committee_stage >= 2;
Q.committee_model = "Autonomous component organizers";
Q.committee_stage += 1;
Q.iran_party_organization += mature ? 1 : 2;
Q.toilers_organization += mature ? 1 : 2;
Q.independent_nationalists_organization += mature ? 1 : 2;
Q.religious_network_organization += mature ? 1 : 2;
Q.organizational_reach += mature ? 0 : 2;
Q.toilers_relation += repeated ? 0 : 1;
Q.religious_network_relation += repeated ? 0 : 1;
if (repeated && mature) Q.iran_party_dissent += 1;
!}

The secretariat divides practical assistance among the component
organizations and asks each to report through its own chain.
{!<span class="term term-social-democratic">!}Toilers' Party{!</span>!} and
{!<span class="term term-religious">!}religious-network{!</span>!} organizers see that cooperation will not erase their
independence.

Every component gains some capacity, but the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} still depends on several
parallel systems when it needs to act together.
[? if committee_stage > 2: The component organizations can preserve the
people they have recruited, but another division of work adds little reach.
The secretariat is now spending more time reconciling parallel instructions. ?]

- @post_event: Continue
